{title: 609 - Am I a Soldier of the Cross?}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #609 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 609}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Am I a soldier [Dm]of the cross,
[C]a [F]follower of the [C]Lamb,
[C7/E]and [F]shall I [Bb]fear [F]to own his [Gm/Bb]cause,
[F/C]or blush [C]to speak [F]his name?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Must I be carried [C7]to [Dm]the skies
[C]on [F]flowery beds of [C]ease,
[C7/E]while [F]others [Bb]fought [F]to win the [Gm/Bb]prize,
[F/C]and sailed [C]through bloody [F]seas?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Are there no foes [C7]for [Dm]me to face?
[C]Must [F]I [Am]not [Gm]stem [F]the flood?
[C7/E]Is [F]this vile [Bb]world [F]a friend to [Gm/Bb]grace,
[F/C]to help [C]me on [F]to God?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Sure I must fight, [C7]if [Dm]I would reign;
[C]increase [Am]my [Gm]courage, [F/C]Lord
[C7/E]I'll [F]bear the [Bb]toil, [F]endure the [Gm/Bb]pain,
[F/C]supported [C]by [F]thy word
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]Thy saints in all [C7]this [Dm]glorious war
[C]shall [F]conquer [Gm]though [F]they die;
[C7/E]they [F]see the [Bb]triumph [F]from afar,
[F/C]by faith [C]they bring [F]it nigh
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[F]When that illustrious [Dm]day shall rise,
[C]and [F]all [Am]thy [Gm]armies [F/C]shine
[C7/E]in [F]robes of [Bb]victory [F]through the [Gm/Bb]skies,
[F/C]the glory [C]shall [F]be thine
{end_of_verse}
